  "_readme": "IMPROVED, INDEPENDENT discrimination test set (does NOT replace data/eval/lr_coverage_cases.json). Motivation: the coverage set only annotated gold-favoring findings (~24), never tested whether the annotator (a) inflates a DISTRACTOR's LR (→ correct branch starves under renormalization), (b) falsely rules OUT the correct branch on a confounder, or (c) fails to rule out a distractor it should; and it had no tree-depth stratification. Here EACH finding carries a full (finding × candidate-branch) EXPECTED-EFFECT matrix, a depth tag (L1 family-routing vs leaf discrimination), and a trap type. Branch keys are leaf DISEASE names so every cell is LR-queryable. Effect vocab (for a finding PRESENT in the vignette): pathognomonic|strong_for|for|weak_for|neutral|weak_against|against|rule_out. trap types: shared_high (alarming but shared → must stay neutral, else false-high starvation), ruleout_distractor (present finding should rule out a distractor), confounder_correct (naive reader might rule OUT the correct dx but it must stay for/neutral), distractor_specific (legit strong_for a distractor), pathognomonic, discriminator (clean leaf discriminator), constitutional (non-specific).",
